#4471 merged every date report into one ticket and marked it known. The cause table does not agree.

The shared parser reads dates month first. A day-first tenant's dates come out flipped. That is `parser`. It is what most of #4471 is.

booking-v3 prints MM/DD/YYYY under the date field. People type what the hint says. The form then reads the date the tenant's way, day first. That is `hint`, a different bug. Those reports were merged into #4471 and have no ticket of their own.

Intake tagged reports from the browser. The cause depends on the tenant: where they are, and which booking form they run. The two disagree.

Reports the desk read as a one-day move stay in the row the tenant puts them in. The table footnotes them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Known was wrong. One ticket per cause. The count is the table, after one id means one report.
</Callout>

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

Each cause is a ticket in this repo. The number on the ticket is the number in that row.

